{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407137-st-tools-for-a-new-ex3-storyteller","id":1407137,"title":"ST Tools for a new EX3 storyteller?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-09T07:38:54-07:00","id":1407137,"title":"ST Tools for a new EX3 storyteller?","content":"Hi everyone, I took about a 3 year hiatus from Exalted because I wasn't much of a fan of the new edition but I recently picked it back up. I'm rereading through the rules again and a lot of the pet peeves I had at the time (merits, range bands, artifact evocations, new exalted types, etc) aren't as annoying to me anymore lol. <br /> <br /> I was wondering if there were any tools people had made to help with range bands, battle groups, combat, social combat, etc that would make it easier for me to handle a new game with basically all new charms, etc. I have &quot;flow charts&quot; for combat and social combat that someone made a long time ago but that's it. Also, this will be an online game so any RPG software suggestions would be greatly appreciated.<br /> <br /> What's your favorite parts of the new system? What parts did you think wouldn't work but work really well? What parts have you houseruled?<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> Tyzerg","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T08:19:00-07:00","id":1407141,"title":"","content":"There's a battle group generator online that takes the stats of creatures from the Core book and the battle group stats you want to factor into them (Drill, Size), and generates their stat block as a battle group. <a href=\"http://colin-fredericks.github.io/ex3-battle-groups\" target=\"_blank\">Here you go.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T09:09:23-07:00","id":1407147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407137-st-tools-for-a-new-ex3-storyteller?p=1407141#post1407141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a battle group generator online that takes the stats of creatures from the Core book and the battle group stats you want to factor into them (Drill, Size), and generates their stat block as a battle group. <a href=\"http://colin-fredericks.github.io/ex3-battle-groups\" target=\"_blank\">Here you go.</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're the man.<br /> <br /> Tyzerg","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T09:45:14-07:00","id":1407151,"title":"","content":"I'm in the process of writing simplified, more D&amp;D 4E-like stat blocks for &quot;typical&quot; Dragon-Blooded antagonists. I'm shooting for 25 moderately powerful E2 antagonists (5 of each Aspect); right now, I'm done with 14. You might find them useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T10:13:49-07:00","id":1407152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407137-st-tools-for-a-new-ex3-storyteller?p=1407151#post1407151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm in the process of writing simplified, more D&amp;D 4E-like stat blocks for &quot;typical&quot; Dragon-Blooded antagonists. I'm shooting for 25 moderately powerful E2 antagonists (5 of each Aspect); right now, I'm done with 14. You might find them useful.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would be great as I also purchased the DB book a few days ago and the 400 page count has me a little scared.<br /> <br /> Tyzerg","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T14:16:24-07:00","id":1407181,"title":"","content":"A heads up that the writing and design quality on books past the Core is vastly improved, largely to the point that I prefer running and playing games with the Dragon-Blooded and Lunars.<br /> <br /> I'd recommend checking out the series of Thousand Sanctioned Beasts on Storyteller's Vault, which make for excellent antagonist splatbooks.<br /> <br /> Also keep your eye out for the upcoming Storyteller's guide: Crucible of Legends, which should have alot of good advice for running Exalted games. Also if you find the minutiae of the system not to your liking keep an eye out for Exalted Essence which is all the 3e exalted in one book with a more streamlined system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 08-09-2020, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T15:19:44-07:00","id":1407194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407137-st-tools-for-a-new-ex3-storyteller?p=1407181#post1407181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A heads up that the writing and design quality on books past the Core is vastly improved, largely to the point that I prefer running and playing games with the Dragon-Blooded and Lunars.<br /> <br /> I'd recommend checking out the series of Thousand Sanctioned Beasts on Storyteller's Vault, which make for excellent antagonist splatbooks.<br /> <br /> Also keep your eye out for the upcoming Storyteller's guide: Crucible of Legends, which should have alot of good advice for running Exalted games. Also if you find the minutiae of the system not to your liking keep an eye out for Exalted Essence which is all the 3e exalted in one book with a more streamlined system.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awesome, I'll check out all those things as they become available. I have the DB hard splat on the way. I also just saw the Exalted useful links thread which I feel will help a lot.<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","user":"Tyzerg","date":". 08-09-2020, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T20:51:29-07:00","id":1407224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407137-st-tools-for-a-new-ex3-storyteller#post1407137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone, I took about a 3 year hiatus from Exalted because I wasn't much of a fan of the new edition but I recently picked it back up. I'm rereading through the rules again and a lot of the pet peeves I had at the time (merits, range bands, artifact evocations, new exalted types, etc) aren't as annoying to me anymore lol.<br /> <br /> I was wondering if there were any tools people had made to help with range bands, battle groups, combat, social combat, etc that would make it easier for me to handle a new game with basically all new charms, etc. I have &quot;flow charts&quot; for combat and social combat that someone made a long time ago but that's it. Also, this will be an online game so any RPG software suggestions would be greatly appreciated.<br /> <br /> What's your favorite parts of the new system? What parts did you think wouldn't work but work really well? What parts have you houseruled?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't used it myself, but <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/</a> is a character creator and manager that I've seen lots of people use before, especially for online games. My group also uses Roll20 as a way to communally see a map and track initiative, but while playing in person we have a little numberline and named tiles that we use for the same purpose. I find that a visual representation of where everyone is in the initiative order is pretty key.<br /> <br /> I think my favourite part of the new system is probably the combat. But the most improved part is probably social influence. It strikes a good balance of letting players with epic social skills be legendary social manipulators, or inspiring people, but it rarely feels like complete mind control.<br /> <br /> <br /> My group has houseruled there to never be more than one Dawn in a game. Somewhat similar to that, I've personally found that the game runs WAY better if not everyone makes their character a combat beast. Like if nobody has less than Dex 3, and combat abilities at 5 with specialties, artifact weapon/armor and half a dozen charms, then stuff goes kind of wonky. From what I can tell, everyone doing that in the game is about the same as if you were running a game in the West, and every single player took Sail 5, half a dozen Sail charms, and an epic artifact dreadnought. You're going to have difficulty making Sail based encounters that are worth busting out the dice for against an entire armada of legendary Solar sailors crewing artifact vessels.<br /> <br /> Also a good houserule I saw recently is to let players get splat-xp, like Solar-xp or Dragon-xp, as many times as they want in a session, but up to a maximum of what they could have earned up to that point. So if one person misses out on their splat xp for three sessions in a row, but then totally kills it in a session that their whole character steals the show, they can make up for it.<br /> <br /> Past that any tools or advise might be better after you've run a few games in the system and see where you're looking to improve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T23:41:23-07:00","id":1407241,"title":"","content":"I cannot recommend roll20 highly enough. The Initiative tracker alone is worth hauling everything in there, but the character sheets and dice rolling capabilities are pretty darn great too.<br /> <br /> As for distances, I use a roll20 page for the 'battle map' that just three concentric circles and a bunch of tiny circles, all on the background layer. They work pretty well to denote who's at what range to what without clogging up the voice chat on somebody else's turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T00:56:07-07:00","id":1407246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407137-st-tools-for-a-new-ex3-storyteller#post1407137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone, I took about a 3 year hiatus from Exalted because I wasn't much of a fan of the new edition but I recently picked it back up. I'm rereading through the rules again and a lot of the pet peeves I had at the time (merits, range bands, artifact evocations, new exalted types, etc) aren't as annoying to me anymore lol. <br /> <br /> I was wondering if there were any tools people had made to help with range bands, battle groups, combat, social combat, etc that would make it easier for me to handle a new game with basically all new charms, etc. I have &amp;quot;flow charts&amp;quot; for combat and social combat that someone made a long time ago but that's it. Also, this will be an online game so any RPG software suggestions would be greatly appreciated.<br /> <br /> What's your favorite parts of the new system? What parts did you think wouldn't work but work really well? What parts have you houseruled?<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> Tyzerg</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a spreadsheet in my signature that marks all scores possibles for NPC's depending on their strength and weaknesse, with examples for each kind of scores. The only lines not cannon are the one directly linked to essence expenditure because I basically divided essence and expenditure by 5 for NPCs to make them easier to track. The rest is taken from the published antagonists so it's cannon (with small adjustment to average some scores)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T09:37:33-07:00","id":1407315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407137-st-tools-for-a-new-ex3-storyteller?p=1407241#post1407241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot recommend roll20 highly enough. The Initiative tracker alone is worth hauling everything in there, but the character sheets and dice rolling capabilities are pretty darn great too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just clarifying, Roll20 has Exalted support now for Initiative order tracking? Or do you just mean using the number options on individual characters to see who has what initiative?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T09:56:13-07:00","id":1407317,"title":"","content":"I can't recommend <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/</a> enough. Great product and great dev support. Also a good little community around it. Makes it really easy to share write ups too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T12:10:23-07:00","id":1407347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407137-st-tools-for-a-new-ex3-storyteller?p=1407315#post1407315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just clarifying, Roll20 has Exalted support now for Initiative order tracking? Or do you just mean using the number options on individual characters to see who has what initiative?</div> </div> </div> </div>If your combatants have tokens, right click those tokens, and select 'add turn'. Then click the clock-looking thing in the upper left (officially called 'turn order'). They should all appear as 0, which you can modify with Join Battle results by left-clicking that 0. Then use the gear in the turn order window, which will bring up some sorting options, you'll want numerical descending. Once a character has taken their turn, use the arrow next to the gear to bump them to the bottom of the list, such that the top of the list is the current turn, and players can see who is on deck after that and prepare accordingly.<br /> <br /> Note that since the turn order is sorted manually, should mid-round Initiative changes happen to higher-Initiative characters that have already taken their turns, they won't be confused as having another turn to take. <br /> <br /> You do need to remember who took the first turn in a round so that you know when to sort again. You also need to manually adjust turns when a character who has not taken their action gains or loses Initiative such that the result changes their order (this is just a click-and-drag operation). When a combatant is eliminated, you can remove them from the order by using the little red trash bin that appears on mouse-over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T09:52:05-07:00","id":1407540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1407137-st-tools-for-a-new-ex3-storyteller?p=1407347#post1407347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your combatants have tokens, right click those tokens, and select 'add turn'. Then click the clock-looking thing in the upper left (officially called 'turn order'). They should all appear as 0, which you can modify with Join Battle results by left-clicking that 0. Then use the gear in the turn order window, which will bring up some sorting options, you'll want numerical descending. Once a character has taken their turn, use the arrow next to the gear to bump them to the bottom of the list, such that the top of the list is the current turn, and players can see who is on deck after that and prepare accordingly.<br /> <br /> Note that since the turn order is sorted manually, should mid-round Initiative changes happen to higher-Initiative characters that have already taken their turns, they won't be confused as having another turn to take.<br /> <br /> You do need to remember who took the first turn in a round so that you know when to sort again. You also need to manually adjust turns when a character who has not taken their action gains or loses Initiative such that the result changes their order (this is just a click-and-drag operation). When a combatant is eliminated, you can remove them from the order by using the little red trash bin that appears on mouse-over.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is really helpful. Thanks! Looks like you can add a &quot;Custom Item&quot; to help you keep track of Top/Bottom of the round. Having to set it lower than your anticipated lowest initiative isn't ideal, but better than nothing! Or I guess you could go highest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T10:53:16-07:00","id":1407553,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure there is a setting in the turn order menu to set a mark at the end of each turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}